ld doing the most  horrific circumstances do you feel angry  about it don't feel angry about what  happened I feel bereft and very very sad  did he know what went on he did in yours  ammonia yep you knew him does it bother  you the idea that John knew him does  that make it worse in your mind is  somehow that they had a relationship and  then this happened to your child and it  makes it more unbelievable because again  I can't I can't imagine how someone who  had been befriended and helped by  someone like Jack could then in a very  fairly calculating way kill them the  only person responsible for what he did  is him so I'm not gonna start lashing  out saying somebody should have stopped  this somebody must be responsible for  this  the police family liaison people advised  us not to do anything on social media I  look Tom I know I suppose I shouldn't  have done I looked on Twitter on the  Saturday morning and already there was  discussion about what happened and what  it meant and  some political reaction immediately  people start jumping on the  criminal-justice bandwagon so you know  advocating longer sentences and harsher  penalties and I knew how passionate was  about rehabilitation and helping people  to redeem themselves and I could already  see it starting to move in the opposite  direction but I just thought it was  important to just push back against that  narrative you had seen that the Prime  Minister had made a statement about  being against slowly release that story  began to build yeah over the weekend  yeah what was required was just you know  dignified a dignified approach you know  whereby the politicians would you know  express their regrets express their  condolences to the to the people  affected and would then get on with  campaigning in the election it wasn't an  election issue where most of us will  were watching this and seeing a tragedy  unfolding in front of our eyes instead  of seeing a tragedy Boris Johnson saw an  opportunity and he wen